    "created_at": "2026-07-27T12:36:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-27T12:36:14Z",
    "body": "I think the downsides of treating all `# xxx: yyy` comments as special are likely to be fairly small, and would save a lot of small pain. There are going to be cases where that will no longer fix normal comments that happen to have a colon in them, and distinguishing those cases might be more trouble than it's worth, but I think the net effect is positive.\n\nI personally also like the suggestion of #3569 of having this configurable.\n\n\nTrying to enumerate common tools would of course work as well, but would be a pain to maintain.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
